APACHE II
APCH1""" ;
    default1:definition "A standardized rating scale developed by Knaus et al in 1985, which is a classification system used to measure severity of disease. This instrument uses a point score system based on physiological measurements, age and previous health status." ;
    default1:reference "Acute Physiology and Chronic Health Evaluation II (APACHE II) (Knaus WA, Draper EA, Wagner DP, Zimmerman JE. APACHE II: a severity of disease classification system. Critical Care Medicine 1985; 13(10):818-29). CDISC believes this instrument to be in the public domain, but you should perform your own assessment.",
        "http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C121005" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf default1:Adult_Sepsis_Diagnostic_Biomarker,
        default1:Adult_Sepsis_Prognostic_Biomarker,
        default1:Clinical_Assessment_Indicator .

